# Sample requests for the JetBrains HTTP client (GoLand). Synthetic data only.
# Start the app first: make run (needs the local infra Postgres, see scripts/README.md).
# Document links point to the sample files `make minio-init` puts into the local MinIO.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Register SOCIAL_MEDIA task → 202, status READY_TO_SUBMIT. Send again → 200.
# requestId = Camunda request (shared); requestGuid = this task (unique, reused on retry).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111","requestGuid":"aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa","operation":"SOCIAL_MEDIA","input":{"iin":"000000000000","fullName":"Тестовый клиент"},"documents":[]}

### Same requestGuid, different input → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111","requestGuid":"aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa","operation":"SOCIAL_MEDIA","input":{"iin":"000000000001","fullName":"Тестовый клиент"},"documents":[]}

### Get task by requestGuid → 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tasks/aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa

### Register REGISTER_COMPARE task → 202, status WAITING_DOCUMENTS
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444","requestGuid":"bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb","operation":"REGISTER_COMPARE","input":{"adjudicate":true},"documents":[{"documentId":"22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222","attstoreUrl":"http://localhost:9000/bpm-bucket/attstore-mock/registry-a.pdf"},{"documentId":"33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333","attstoreUrl":"http://localhost:9000/bpm-bucket/attstore-mock/registry-b.pdf"}]}

### REGISTER_COMPARE with one document → 422 VALIDATION_ERROR, documents INVALID_COUNT
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555555","requestGuid":"cccccccc-cccc-4ccc-8ccc-cccccccccccc","operation":"REGISTER_COMPARE","input":{},"documents":[{"documentId":"22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222","attstoreUrl":"http://localhost:9000/bpm-bucket/attstore-mock/registry-a.pdf"}]}

### Unknown field → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR, extra UNKNOWN_FIELD
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"66666666-6666-4666-8666-666666666666","requestGuid":"dddddddd-dddd-4ddd-8ddd-dddddddddddd","operation":"SOCIAL_MEDIA","input":{"iin":"000000000000","fullName":"x"},"documents":[],"extra":1}

### Missing task → 404 TASK_NOT_FOUND
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tasks/99999999-9999-4999-8999-999999999999

### Same Camunda request, same documents, new task (new requestGuid) → 202
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444","requestGuid":"eeeeeeee-eeee-4eee-8eee-eeeeeeeeeeee","operation":"REGISTER_COMPARE","input":{"adjudicate":false},"documents":[{"documentId":"22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222","attstoreUrl":"http://localhost:9000/bpm-bucket/attstore-mock/registry-a.pdf"},{"documentId":"33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333","attstoreUrl":"http://localhost:9000/bpm-bucket/attstore-mock/registry-b.pdf"}]}

### Readiness: 200 when the database is reachable, 503 otherwise
GET {{host}}/health/readiness

### ─── Worker API (worker.Request): documents to copy Attstore → S3. Mock for now. ───

### Claim documents → 200 with up to `limit` demo documents and fresh claim tokens
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/documents/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"workerId":"worker-request-local","limit":2}

> {% client.global.set("docId", response.body.items[0].id); client.global.set("claimToken", response.body.items[0].claimToken); %}

### Renew the claim (heartbeat) → 200 with a new claimUntil
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/documents/{{docId}}/renew
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{claimToken}}"}

### Report a successful copy → 200 {"applied":true}
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/documents/{{docId}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{claimToken}}","s3Uri":"s3://ai-input/tasks/demo/0","sizeBytes":123456,"checksumSha256":"9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08"}

### Report a failed copy → 200 {"applied":true}
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/documents/{{docId}}/failure
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{claimToken}}","code":"SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","message":"Attstore returned 503","retryable":true}

### Wrong claim token → 409 CLAIM_LOST
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/documents/{{docId}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000","s3Uri":"s3://ai-input/tasks/demo/0","sizeBytes":1,"checksumSha256":"9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08"}

### ─── Worker API (worker.Request): send ready tasks to AI. Mock for now. ───

### Claim a task to send → 200 with an attempt (attemptId = AI task_id), its input and S3 files
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/submissions/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"workerId":"worker-request-local","limit":1}

> {% client.global.set("attemptId", response.body.items[0].attemptId); client.global.set("submissionToken", response.body.items[0].claimToken); %}

### Renew while the POST to AI is in progress → 200 with a new claimUntil
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/submissions/{{attemptId}}/renew
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{submissionToken}}"}

### AI accepted the task → 200 {"applied":true}
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/submissions/{{attemptId}}/outcome
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{submissionToken}}","outcome":"ACCEPTED","remoteStatus":"QUEUED"}

### No reliable answer from AI (timeout) → 200; polling will find out
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/submissions/{{attemptId}}/outcome
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{submissionToken}}","outcome":"UNKNOWN","failure":{"code":"AI_TIMEOUT","message":"No response from AI within 30s"}}

### AI refused the task → 200; the AI place is freed
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/submissions/{{attemptId}}/outcome
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{submissionToken}}","outcome":"REJECTED","failure":{"code":"INVALID_INPUT","message":"AI rejected the files"}}

### ─── Worker API (worker.Response): check the status of tasks at AI. Mock for now. ───

### Claim status checks → 200 with attempts to check (attemptId = AI task_id)
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/polls/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"workerId":"worker-response-local","limit":5}

> {% client.global.set("pollAttemptId", response.body.items[0].attemptId); client.global.set("pollToken", response.body.items[0].claimToken); %}

### AI: still working → 200
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/polls/{{pollAttemptId}}/observation
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{pollToken}}","outcome":"PROCESSING"}

### AI: done, with its result JSON → 200
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/polls/{{pollAttemptId}}/observation
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{pollToken}}","outcome":"SUCCEEDED","result":{"summary":{"counts":{"both":12,"review":1}},"extraction_complete":true,"report_url":"https://s3.example/reports/r.docx","report_url_excel":"https://s3.example/reports/r.xlsx"}}

### AI: finished with a business error → 200
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/polls/{{pollAttemptId}}/observation
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{pollToken}}","outcome":"FAILED","failure":{"code":"EXTRACTION_FAILED","message":"Could not read document 2"}}

### AI: task not found → 200
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/polls/{{pollAttemptId}}/observation
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{pollToken}}","outcome":"NOT_FOUND"}

### No usable answer (timeout) → 200
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/polls/{{pollAttemptId}}/observation
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{pollToken}}","outcome":"TECHNICAL_ERROR","failure":{"code":"AI_TIMEOUT","message":"No response from AI within 10s"}}

### ─── Worker API (worker.Response): deliver final results to BPM via Kafka. Mock for now. ───

### Claim results to deliver → 200 with topic, key and the ready message
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/results/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{"workerId":"worker-response-local","limit":5}

> {% client.global.set("resultGuid", response.body.items[0].requestGuid); client.global.set("resultToken", response.body.items[0].claimToken); %}

### Kafka confirmed (broker ACK) → 200
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/results/{{resultGuid}}/published
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{resultToken}}"}

### Kafka did not accept it → 200; tried again later, never dropped
POST {{host}}/internal/v1/results/{{resultGuid}}/failure
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimToken":"{{resultToken}}","failure":{"code":"KAFKA_UNAVAILABLE","message":"No broker ACK within 10s"}}
